.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-db-stats 1  "tapectl-db-stats " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-db\-stats \- Show database statistics, and what each table weighs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl db stats\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show database statistics, and what each table weighs
.PP
The database\*(Aqs size, then every table\*(Aqs row count and size, largest first. The journals (`health_logs`, `verification_results`, `events`, the forensic journals) are never pruned, so this is how their growth is seen. Sizes are measured with SQLite\*(Aqs dbstat table when the build has it (the bundled build does) and estimated otherwise; the output says which (`size_method` in `\-\-json`).
.PP
Then each journal\*(Aqs growth over the trailing 90 days, fastest first: the rows dated in the window, the bytes they take, and that pace over a year (`journal_growth` in `\-\-json`). The row count is exact; the bytes are derived, the bytes in use on the table\*(Aqs pages shared among its rows by stored length. A catalog younger than 90 days is paced over its own age, from its oldest journal row.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No live progress on stderr. Long operations (stage create, volume write/resume/verify/read\-slices, restore) still write their session log under <home>/logs/
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, stage reports. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, stage\-reports, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
